# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run a managed workflow one time for each set of inputs, collect the results, and stay under the active job limit."
msgstr "Esegui un workflow gestito una volta per ogni insieme di input, raccogli i risultati e resta entro il limite di job attivi."

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run a parameter sweep"
msgstr "Eseguire uno sweep di parametri"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"guides/run-parameter-sweep.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/*\n"
"  DO NOT EDIT THIS CELL!!!\n"
"  This cell's content is generated automatically by a script. Anything you add\n"
"  here will be removed next time the notebook is run. To add new content, create\n"
"  a new cell before or after this one.\n"
"*/}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Package versions\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Versioni dei pacchetti\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The code on this page was developed using the following requirements.\n"
"We recommend using these versions or newer.\n"
msgstr ""
"Il codice in questa pagina è stato sviluppato usando i seguenti requisiti.\n"
"Ti consigliamo di usare queste versioni o successive.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"A parameter sweep works like a Slurm job array. Call `run()` one time for each set of inputs, and the jobs run at the same time, each on its own node. Use the same pattern for any batch of independent inputs, such as one job for each molecule or each backend. Jobs cannot send data to each other, so split the work into independent inputs.\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Uno sweep di parametri funziona come un job array di Slurm. Chiama `run()` una volta per ogni insieme di input e i job vengono eseguiti contemporaneamente, ciascuno sul proprio nodo. Usa lo stesso schema per qualsiasi gruppo di input indipendenti, come un job per ogni molecola o per ogni backend. I job non possono scambiarsi dati, quindi suddividi il lavoro in input indipendenti.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The examples on this page use the workflow from [Run a managed workflow](/guides/run-managed-workflow), which reads one angle, `theta`:\n"
msgstr "Gli esempi in questa pagina usano il workflow di [Eseguire un workflow gestito](/guides/run-managed-workflow), che legge un angolo, `theta`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Start the jobs {#start-the-jobs}"
msgstr "Avviare i job {#start-the-jobs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Get the workflow by its title, and call `run()` one time for each input. Save the job IDs to a file:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"Ottieni il workflow tramite il suo titolo e chiama `run()` una volta per ogni input. Salva gli ID dei job in un file:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Check every input first.** If the workflow has an [argument schema](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#best-practice-validate-arguments-with-a-schema), call `validate_arguments()` on each input before the loop.\n"
msgstr "**Controlla prima ogni input.** Se il workflow ha uno [schema degli argomenti](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#best-practice-validate-arguments-with-a-schema), chiama `validate_arguments()` su ogni input prima del ciclo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Save the job IDs to a file.** You can then collect the results from a new session.\n"
msgstr "**Salva gli ID dei job in un file.** Potrai poi raccogliere i risultati da una nuova sessione.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Give each run's files a unique name.** All runs share the workflow's file storage. See [Best practice: give each run's files a unique name](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows#best-practice-give-each-runs-files-a-unique-name).\n"
msgstr "**Assegna un nome univoco ai file di ogni esecuzione.** Tutte le esecuzioni condividono l'archiviazione file del workflow. Consulta [Best practice: assegna un nome univoco ai file di ogni esecuzione](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows#best-practice-give-each-runs-files-a-unique-name).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Stay under the [active job limit](#active-job-limit).** A managed workflow does not queue jobs over the limit, so when you reach it, start more jobs only after earlier jobs end.\n"
msgstr "**Resta entro il [limite di job attivi](#active-job-limit).** Un workflow gestito non mette in coda i job oltre il limite, quindi quando lo raggiungi, avvia altri job solo dopo che quelli precedenti sono terminati.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Collect the results {#collect-the-results}"
msgstr "Raccogliere i risultati {#collect-the-results}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Get each job by its ID, and catch failed jobs so that one failure does not stop the loop:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"Ottieni ogni job tramite il suo ID e intercetta i job falliti in modo che un errore non interrompa il ciclo:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To rerun the inputs that failed, call `run()` again with the same arguments.\n"
msgstr "Per rieseguire gli input che sono falliti, chiama di nuovo `run()` con gli stessi argomenti.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Active job limit {#active-job-limit}"
msgstr "Limite di job attivi {#active-job-limit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can have up to 50 jobs that are queued, initializing, running, or canceling at the same time. This limit counts all of your jobs, including jobs of other workflows. If you exceed this limit, `run()` raises a `QiskitServerlessException` and does not create or queue the job:\n"
msgstr "Puoi avere fino a 50 job in coda, in inizializzazione, in esecuzione o in annullamento contemporaneamente. Questo limite conta tutti i tuoi job, inclusi quelli di altri workflow. Se superi questo limite, `run()` solleva una `QiskitServerlessException` e non crea né mette in coda il job:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr "Passaggi successivi {#next-steps}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Recommendations\">\n"
"- [Manage files across runs](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows) to share input files between runs and give each run's files a unique name.\n"
"- [Choose a compute profile](/guides/managed-workflow-compute-profiles) to run each job of the sweep on a size that matches its input.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Raccomandazioni\">\n"
"- [Gestire i file tra le esecuzioni](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows) per condividere i file di input tra le esecuzioni e assegnare un nome univoco ai file di ciascuna.\n"
"- [Scegliere un profilo di calcolo](/guides/managed-workflow-compute-profiles) per eseguire ogni job dello sweep con una dimensione adatta al suo input.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
